1
00:02:04,430 --> 00:02:09,060
NO ANIMALS WERE HARMED
DURING THE FILMING OF THIS MOVIE

2
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:44,340
Osman has gone mad. Does this man thinks
he can defeat us with so little numbers?

3
00:03:07,860 --> 00:03:09,930
You treacherous dog!

4
00:03:23,640 --> 00:03:24,920
Archers!

5
00:04:17,019 --> 00:04:19,440
2 DAYS AGO

6
00:05:50,530 --> 00:05:51,540
Pretty lamb...

7
00:05:52,570 --> 00:05:53,510
Come.

8
00:06:00,900 --> 00:06:04,900
Oh, pretty lamb! You are a pretty lamb!

9
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:12,860
Look, wolf brother is here too.

10
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:21,870
Come, wolf brother.

11
00:06:31,980 --> 00:06:34,870
A Brother who loves being
the fog's companion.

12
00:06:35,090 --> 00:06:37,880
Brother who becomes
the guide on the roads.

13
00:07:01,690 --> 00:07:05,840
My loves, the mystery has been solved.

14
00:07:06,400 --> 00:07:08,290
The mystery has been solved!

15
00:07:08,690 --> 00:07:11,130
The mystery has
been solved in Hira!

16
00:07:12,190 --> 00:07:15,510
He read, he read!
The orphan of Mekkah read!

17
00:07:16,190 --> 00:07:21,690
Get out of the way, for he comes!
Muhammed, whose name is beautiful comes!

18
00:07:28,050 --> 00:07:32,050
Wreathe, wreathe...

19
00:07:32,420 --> 00:07:36,510
Wreathe your lover! He read, he read!

20
00:07:37,200 --> 00:07:40,440
The orphan of Mekkah read!
He read, and Kisrâ wavered.

21
00:07:40,540 --> 00:07:43,130
He read, and the fire of the
Zoroastrians extinguished.

22
00:07:43,130 --> 00:07:47,140
He read, and the tyranny ended
and the world saw the light!

23
00:07:47,680 --> 00:07:51,680
What's coming, is coming!
What's coming, is coming!

24
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:56,000
What's coming, is coming!

25
00:08:30,780 --> 00:08:36,159
There are roads that make the heart clear,
and the mind strong.

26
00:08:36,970 --> 00:08:40,970
My heart is clear, and my mind is clean!

27
00:08:41,970 --> 00:08:46,880
You didn't exist, then you did.
You existed, then you didn't.

28
00:08:47,350 --> 00:08:52,510
Neither existing, or non-existing,
what matters is union.

29
00:08:52,940 --> 00:08:57,510
And the union is a great state.
Hail to the men of state!

30
00:08:57,510 --> 00:08:59,450
Hail to the men of state!

31
00:08:59,600 --> 00:09:01,140
Hail to the state!

32
00:09:01,650 --> 00:09:03,270
Hail!

33
00:09:03,270 --> 00:09:07,620
This gate, is of state.
This gate, is of men.

34
00:09:07,840 --> 00:09:14,540
With an invulnerable gate, unbreakable
wrist, heart is what a man needs.

35
00:09:15,370 --> 00:09:19,370
Threes, sevens, forties!

36
00:09:19,910 --> 00:09:24,040
The ones who became
one in forty! Hail to you!

37
00:09:25,190 --> 00:09:28,250
May our state endure!

38
00:09:28,730 --> 00:09:31,400
May the world see the light!

39
00:09:31,500 --> 00:09:35,500
May the marching men
become a state to the world!

40
00:09:35,580 --> 00:09:37,370
May he become the state!

41
00:10:51,660 --> 00:10:53,470
Welcome.

42
00:10:54,520 --> 00:10:56,190
Thank you.

43
00:10:58,650 --> 00:11:00,030
Come, sit.

44
00:11:35,290 --> 00:11:38,240
Pretty lamb...

45
00:11:47,220 --> 00:11:49,590
Allah created humans.

46
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:54,730
He gave them wisdom, heart.

47
00:11:55,940 --> 00:12:01,520
Mind's ornament is tongue, and the
tongue's ornaments are words.

48
00:12:02,480 --> 00:12:05,970
I heard. It's the truth.

49
00:12:06,210 --> 00:12:11,010
Everything that existed from
nothing, will cease to exist.

50
00:12:11,880 --> 00:12:17,440
This thing you call life will
also pass like the wind.

51
00:12:18,320 --> 00:12:21,320
I heard. It's the truth.

52
00:12:22,350 --> 00:12:30,070
But, if one can hold both of his worlds
together in balance, one will find peace.

53
00:12:32,890 --> 00:12:36,530
A bey is great if he obeys the tradition.

54
00:12:37,730 --> 00:12:41,040
If Allah gives a Bey a blessing.

55
00:12:41,230 --> 00:12:49,390
That Bey, his people and
his state will be happy.

56
00:12:50,330 --> 00:12:52,620
I heard. It's the truth.

57
00:12:53,550 --> 00:12:58,410
Now is the time to
unlock the heart's lock...

58
00:12:59,040 --> 00:13:03,040
... and to sheathe wisdom's sword.

59
00:13:04,540 --> 00:13:06,240
I've been called to peacefulness.

60
00:13:07,660 --> 00:13:10,170
I came to the council, that's
whiter than the white.

61
00:13:10,790 --> 00:13:14,790
My mission is to reburn our fire.

62
00:13:15,330 --> 00:13:18,960
Both you, and your aim is known.

63
00:13:19,520 --> 00:13:22,950
But do you know yourself?

64
00:13:28,170 --> 00:13:29,760
Forgive me if I made a mistake.

65
00:13:30,400 --> 00:13:33,650
One who understands, understands.
One who knows, know.

66
00:13:34,260 --> 00:13:38,260
The one who knows, and
understands, gets what one wants.

67
00:13:38,810 --> 00:13:45,640
From now on, the sword you carry, the
horse you ride, the bed that you sleep...

68
00:13:45,640 --> 00:13:50,100
the road you walk, the dream that
you dreamt is not yours.

69
00:13:50,570 --> 00:13:54,570
The time is not yours,
the place is not yours.

70
00:13:54,590 --> 00:13:58,910
The son is not yours,
The breath is not yours!

71
00:14:00,930 --> 00:14:02,380
Then whose are they?

72
00:14:02,960 --> 00:14:07,630
They are nation's. They are nation's.
They are nation's.

73
00:14:15,590 --> 00:14:18,700
The world is on fire.

74
00:14:19,730 --> 00:14:22,720
It's crumbling, shattered.

75
00:14:23,320 --> 00:14:28,010
The devil's army is fighting, killing.

76
00:14:28,790 --> 00:14:33,790
The people are waiting for a hope from us,
they want us to act!

77
00:14:35,500 --> 00:14:37,040
How do we do that?

78
00:14:37,490 --> 00:14:41,710
By being a Turk, staying in Islam.

79
00:14:41,920 --> 00:14:46,510
That is not anyone's,
but of a wise man's job.

80
00:14:47,780 --> 00:14:52,850
Hail to my ancestor Oghuz,
to Saltuk Buğra Han...

81
00:14:53,680 --> 00:14:57,680
... and from Saltuk Buğra
Han, to Alparslan...

82
00:14:57,860 --> 00:15:02,950
... and to countless soldiers of heart,

83
00:15:04,090 --> 00:15:11,030
And, may all our greetings go to the
Sultan of the worlds, Prophet Muhammad...

84
00:15:11,030 --> 00:15:14,110
... and his followers.

85
00:15:19,300 --> 00:15:22,450
Osman, son of Ertuğrul.

86
00:15:24,190 --> 00:15:27,390
The devil's army is burning the world.

87
00:15:29,080 --> 00:15:32,250
The Turk's army builds order.

88
00:15:34,590 --> 00:15:41,800
We will build such a state, that in it,
the wolf and the lamb will be brothers.

89
00:15:42,910 --> 00:15:48,960
We will build such a state, that we will
find white hair in the white milk.

90
00:15:49,630 --> 00:15:54,320
We will build such a state,
that it will endure forever.

91
00:15:54,830 --> 00:15:58,830
May my blood and life
be sacrificed for this state.

92
00:16:00,420 --> 00:16:05,250
May my mind and heart be for this state.

93
00:16:07,130 --> 00:16:12,800
Now our legend begins.
You've come and we've met.

94
00:16:13,340 --> 00:16:15,560
We have met, and we have dreamt.

95
00:16:15,810 --> 00:16:22,050
Our first mission is to make
our people dream of a state.

96
00:16:22,990 --> 00:16:28,580
May this be such a
dream, that 72 nations...

97
00:16:28,760 --> 00:16:35,210
... 7 weathers, 4 corner
unite under that dream.

98
00:16:37,140 --> 00:16:43,550
May this be such a dream,
that everyone will find peace.

99
00:16:57,400 --> 00:16:59,910
We passed this summer in Domaniç too.

100
00:17:00,020 --> 00:17:03,400
Time runs fast.
At least our animals are fed.

101
00:17:03,590 --> 00:17:09,230
And our women gathered all the plants.
They prepared winter supplies.

102
00:17:20,810 --> 00:17:24,220
Who is it? Yusuf, is that you?

103
00:17:26,390 --> 00:17:31,380
I'm in a deep well. Hasan, it's you!

104
00:17:33,640 --> 00:17:37,950
Who is it? Whose hands are those?

105
00:17:40,890 --> 00:17:45,460
These hands, these iron holding hands...

106
00:17:46,350 --> 00:17:49,980
My little blacksmith, beautiful
named Ahmet's hands!

107
00:18:04,780 --> 00:18:09,420
I kiss your flower gathering hands.

108
00:18:09,890 --> 00:18:13,720
My valiant Ahmet. Gonca Hatun!

109
00:18:13,720 --> 00:18:15,850
Give Ahmet his gift.

110
00:18:19,530 --> 00:18:21,240
Here.

111
00:18:28,980 --> 00:18:30,640
Are you prepared?

112
00:18:31,090 --> 00:18:35,850
I helped my father but the work
is not done. There is a lot of work left.

113
00:18:36,180 --> 00:18:39,260
He said we can move only
after the caravan leaves.

114
00:18:40,460 --> 00:18:42,000
Why is that?

115
00:18:42,460 --> 00:18:47,490
Father said, if my mother was
here, it would be easier.

116
00:19:02,730 --> 00:19:06,730
Why are we here for, my Ahmet?
We will help, of course.

117
00:19:07,990 --> 00:19:12,170
Gonca, you can go help,
I will come after I'm finished here.

118
00:19:12,930 --> 00:19:15,630
Come Ahmet. Let's go.

119
00:19:16,890 --> 00:19:19,490
Can we race? Who would win?

120
00:19:19,490 --> 00:19:20,410
Come on then!

121
00:19:32,620 --> 00:19:35,520
The children smell like heaven, my Bala.

122
00:19:36,090 --> 00:19:40,090
Ahmet is an orphan. My heart
hurts everytime I look at him.

123
00:19:42,130 --> 00:19:46,700
That's because your soft
heart wants to be a mother.

124
00:19:48,010 --> 00:19:52,010
It has been some time that
you've been married to Osman, girl.

125
00:19:54,010 --> 00:19:59,340
The time for you to hold your own
child on your hands has come already.

126
00:20:02,360 --> 00:20:05,200
And, Osman is a son of Bey.

127
00:20:06,030 --> 00:20:09,910
He can't be without a child.

128
00:20:11,130 --> 00:20:13,160
Especially a boy,

129
00:20:16,800 --> 00:20:19,200
The one who gives and
takes is Allah, Hazal Hatun.

130
00:20:19,350 --> 00:20:22,500
Of course, of course.

131
00:20:23,060 --> 00:20:24,140
But...

132
00:20:27,110 --> 00:20:28,660
... you should try harder.

133
00:20:30,140 --> 00:20:32,090
If it's not happening, find a cure.

134
00:20:33,280 --> 00:20:39,850
Look, people talks. They say
Bala Hatun won't have a baby.

135
00:20:41,080 --> 00:20:44,970
They might talk to Osman too.
They are men.

136
00:20:45,360 --> 00:20:47,180
Their patience is short.

137
00:20:49,360 --> 00:20:54,810
You might share your tent with
another woman in an instant.

138
00:20:59,380 --> 00:21:02,780
If it is my destiny, I will live it too.

139
00:21:22,200 --> 00:21:26,200
I am like your mother, girl.
If you have a problem, tell me.

140
00:21:26,380 --> 00:21:28,730
It's also my responsibility
to seek a remedy.

141
00:21:31,720 --> 00:21:36,470
First we move the caravan to Söğüt,
then we can talk about it later.

142
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:40,290
Inshallah.

143
00:21:48,910 --> 00:21:52,470
Mashallah to my lion, mashallah!

144
00:21:52,760 --> 00:21:55,950
My Ahmet, where are
you going in such a hurry.

145
00:21:56,180 --> 00:22:00,180
Boran Alp, leave us,
we will go to my father.

146
00:22:00,490 --> 00:22:03,170
I can help too, let's go.

147
00:22:03,300 --> 00:22:06,560
Gonca Hatun will help, thank you.

148
00:22:06,840 --> 00:22:09,650
It's enough for soldiers
to do their own job.

149
00:22:23,780 --> 00:22:26,720
Thank you, Ahmet Alp, thank you.

150
00:22:29,270 --> 00:22:30,330
Come here.

151
00:22:31,460 --> 00:22:33,850
Come on, my lion.

152
00:22:49,660 --> 00:22:53,100
My Bey will be there until
we migrate, right brother?

153
00:22:53,180 --> 00:22:54,810
He will, inshallah, he will.

154
00:22:55,010 --> 00:22:56,090
Inshallah.

155
00:23:00,260 --> 00:23:02,500
Father, father!

156
00:23:03,510 --> 00:23:05,150
May your father die for you!

157
00:23:06,010 --> 00:23:09,550
I've brought you Gonca Hatun,
so we can prepare faster.

158
00:23:09,550 --> 00:23:11,950
- Thank you, sister.
- It's nothing, brother Hasan.

159
00:23:12,300 --> 00:23:14,350
Come on, let's get to work.

160
00:23:22,710 --> 00:23:25,440
- Ambush!
- Ambush!

161
00:23:36,780 --> 00:23:39,240
- Ambush!
- Ambush!

162
00:24:12,860 --> 00:24:14,980
Come on! Get the spears!

163
00:24:17,680 --> 00:24:20,570
Leave no one alive! Attack!

164
00:25:47,140 --> 00:25:48,660
Ahmet!

165
00:26:37,600 --> 00:26:39,330
Leave your weapons.

166
00:26:55,530 --> 00:26:57,450
I will leave them to you.

167
00:27:59,370 --> 00:28:01,940
This year's onions are
rather bitter, uncle.

168
00:28:09,610 --> 00:28:13,840
Would there be fruitfulness where
the Mongol walks, nephew?

169
00:28:14,240 --> 00:28:20,990
Inshallah, when those jackals leave our
soil, onions will be the same as before.

170
00:28:25,800 --> 00:28:29,800
I have around 50 Frank soldiers...

171
00:28:30,520 --> 00:28:35,710
... and Nökers that escaped
from Geyhatu's wrath.

172
00:28:40,680 --> 00:28:44,680
They are looking for someone
to sell their swords like me.

173
00:28:44,770 --> 00:28:48,280
Why would we hire
men like you, Cerkutay?

174
00:28:50,820 --> 00:28:54,280
I've heard that you took Kulucahisar.

175
00:28:56,830 --> 00:28:58,170
Byzantium is hunting you.

176
00:29:01,410 --> 00:29:04,390
And Geyhatu is also looking for you.

177
00:29:06,860 --> 00:29:09,760
You need warriors like us.

178
00:29:14,810 --> 00:29:18,970
Before we sell our swords to your enemies...

179
00:29:22,610 --> 00:29:24,490
... for old times' sake...

180
00:29:27,870 --> 00:29:29,990
... I came to you first.

181
00:29:30,270 --> 00:29:32,530
I give an offer to you first!

182
00:30:04,080 --> 00:30:06,610
Ahmet! Ahmet!

183
00:30:09,420 --> 00:30:11,590
Father! Father!

184
00:30:12,850 --> 00:30:15,770
Father! Father!

185
00:30:26,150 --> 00:30:28,090
Come here, don't run!

186
00:30:49,360 --> 00:30:51,020
Bala Hatun!

187
00:30:54,290 --> 00:30:55,630
Bala Hatun!

188
00:31:07,690 --> 00:31:09,050
Ahmet'

189
00:31:09,270 --> 00:31:10,410
Let go!

190
00:31:15,190 --> 00:31:18,530
Let me go! Bala Hatun!

191
00:31:26,520 --> 00:31:33,150
We have nothing to do with the bandits
who run from the battle, and betray...

192
00:31:33,850 --> 00:31:35,280
... their own army.

193
00:31:46,870 --> 00:31:53,120
No problem. I made
my offer, I will not insist.

194
00:32:01,640 --> 00:32:05,130
- My Bey!
- What is it, Saltuk? What happened?

195
00:32:05,150 --> 00:32:08,140
Lord Alexis attacked the ones
who were returning.

196
00:32:08,140 --> 00:32:11,040
Women and children,
we've lost so many, my Bey.

197
00:32:11,290 --> 00:32:14,840
What are you talking about, Saltuk?
Where is Hazal and Bala Hatun?

198
00:32:15,130 --> 00:32:19,130
The soldier who brought
the news said he doesn't know.

199
00:32:22,680 --> 00:32:28,290
So the whole world wants to come to us.
Then let them come!

200
00:32:31,720 --> 00:32:36,830
And get these out of Söğüt.
If I ever see them again...

201
00:33:29,850 --> 00:33:31,810
Help the wounded!

202
00:33:35,660 --> 00:33:37,480
Help the wounded!

203
00:33:39,690 --> 00:33:42,740
For the love of Allah, water!

204
00:33:49,860 --> 00:33:51,090
Come on!

205
00:35:23,400 --> 00:35:25,490
In the name of Allah.

206
00:35:30,680 --> 00:35:33,260
Castle of İnegöl

207
00:36:18,130 --> 00:36:23,900
Ahmet! Ahmet! Ahmet!
Ahmet Alp! Ahmet Alp!

208
00:36:26,460 --> 00:36:31,560
A valiant doesn't give up.
A warrior doesn't lose hope.

209
00:36:31,560 --> 00:36:33,770
Osman Bey will save us, my lion.

210
00:36:34,000 --> 00:36:35,670
He will save us.

211
00:36:37,540 --> 00:36:40,030
I'm a warrior of Osman Bey.

212
00:36:40,650 --> 00:36:43,700
How could I bow down to these craven?

213
00:36:44,000 --> 00:36:47,370
-Mashallah. Mashallah, my lion.
-Silence!

214
00:37:10,700 --> 00:37:13,790
We are the warriors of Osman Bey.

215
00:37:15,970 --> 00:37:17,970
We are the warriors of Osman Bey.

216
00:37:18,740 --> 00:37:22,610
-We are the warriors of Osman Bey.
-We are the warriors of Osman Bey.

217
00:37:23,380 --> 00:37:27,710
-We are the warriors of Osman Bey.
-We are the warriors of Osman Bey.

218
00:37:28,010 --> 00:37:31,290
-We are the warriors of Osman Bey.
-We are the warriors of Osman Bey.

219
00:37:31,470 --> 00:37:35,680
-We are the warriors of Osman Bey.
-We are the warriors of Osman Bey.

220
00:37:35,950 --> 00:37:40,110
-We are the warriors of Osman Bey.
-We are the warriors of Osman Bey.

221
00:37:40,210 --> 00:37:44,160
-We are the warriors of Osman Bey.
-We are the warriors of Osman Bey.

222
00:37:44,430 --> 00:37:48,820
-We are the warriors of Osman Bey.
-We are the warriors of Osman Bey.

223
00:37:49,230 --> 00:37:52,820
-We are the warriors of Osman Bey.
-We are the warriors of Osman Bey.

224
00:37:52,880 --> 00:38:01,350
-We are the warriors of Osman Bey.
-We are the warriors of Osman Bey.

225
00:38:01,450 --> 00:38:05,860
-We are the warriors of Osman Bey.
-We are the warriors of Osman Bey.

226
00:38:06,050 --> 00:38:10,110
-We are the warriors of Osman Bey.
-We are the warriors of Osman Bey.

227
00:38:32,640 --> 00:38:35,020
Father!
Father!

228
00:38:54,410 --> 00:38:56,070
Hey!

229
00:39:32,460 --> 00:39:36,060
Long-suffering and enduring people
of İnegöl!

230
00:39:38,240 --> 00:39:40,770
You lost your sleep for too long...

231
00:39:41,490 --> 00:39:43,490
...you were waiting in fear
for too long...

232
00:39:43,490 --> 00:39:47,080
...you were grieved to hear what
happened in Kulucahisar.

233
00:39:48,020 --> 00:39:51,660
Osman the Cruel and his men burned our
brothers alive!

234
00:39:51,930 --> 00:39:55,710
They killed babies in their mothers'
bellies. Like it wasn't enough...

235
00:39:55,710 --> 00:39:57,380
...they burned our churches!

236
00:39:57,650 --> 00:40:01,600
Every place these barbarians stepped on,
turned into a blood bath.

237
00:40:03,920 --> 00:40:09,210
I, the Lord of İnegöl,
Alexis...

238
00:40:09,750 --> 00:40:12,770
...I brought you peace!

239
00:40:13,450 --> 00:40:18,260
I took our revenge from those barbarians
in such a way that...

240
00:40:18,720 --> 00:40:21,400
...they won't forget it until their
last breaths.

241
00:40:21,730 --> 00:40:26,180
They paid for all the pain we suffered!

242
00:40:30,060 --> 00:40:33,920
Lying pander...
Lying pander!

243
00:40:41,560 --> 00:40:44,030
Where is Osman?

244
00:40:46,040 --> 00:40:47,460
Where is Osman?

245
00:40:48,520 --> 00:40:53,900
We want to drink wine from Osman's
skull!

246
00:41:01,270 --> 00:41:03,400
Allahu Akbar.

247
00:41:08,920 --> 00:41:10,740
Allahu Akbar.

248
00:41:12,930 --> 00:41:18,130
I promise you, the head of that barbarian
will be on our pike!

249
00:41:18,690 --> 00:41:24,650
I promise you, the castles that those
devils occupied will be ours again!

250
00:41:46,200 --> 00:41:48,810
This isn't the place, take them away,
come on!

251
00:41:53,750 --> 00:41:57,050
-What's wrong, Göktuğ?
-My Bey.

252
00:41:59,690 --> 00:42:01,760
We were raided in the Domaniç uplands.

253
00:42:02,750 --> 00:42:05,720
What are you saying? Who?
What panders?

254
00:42:05,780 --> 00:42:08,700
Alexis. Lord of İnegöl.

255
00:42:09,980 --> 00:42:11,940
What're our casualties?

256
00:42:14,400 --> 00:42:15,630
Heavy, my bey.

257
00:42:19,480 --> 00:42:21,050
Come on!
Come on!

258
00:42:40,600 --> 00:42:42,100
Where was my uncle then?

259
00:42:42,710 --> 00:42:45,730
Where was Gündüz Bey?
Where were the soldiers?

260
00:42:46,550 --> 00:42:48,730
What were they doing?

261
00:42:52,620 --> 00:42:56,010
-Hang on. Hang on, brothers! Hang on!
-Thank you.

262
00:42:57,340 --> 00:43:00,150
We will get over this too, inshallah.

263
00:43:08,570 --> 00:43:10,230
-My bey.
-Huh?

264
00:43:14,570 --> 00:43:15,790
Speak!

265
00:43:16,240 --> 00:43:17,610
Bala Hatun...

266
00:43:18,100 --> 00:43:21,000
-What happened?
-Bala Hatun is wounded, my bey.

267
00:43:56,230 --> 00:43:57,260
Bala!

268
00:44:03,640 --> 00:44:05,950
Bala! Bala!

269
00:44:09,770 --> 00:44:12,520
Mother, my heart is burning.
Tell me she is all right!

270
00:44:14,060 --> 00:44:16,690
Thank Allah, our girl is in
perfect health.

271
00:44:20,100 --> 00:44:21,490
Bala...

272
00:44:23,790 --> 00:44:24,850
Osman...

273
00:44:26,550 --> 00:44:27,990
Osman...

274
00:44:28,430 --> 00:44:30,920
Bala! My love.

275
00:44:31,540 --> 00:44:32,690
My heart.

276
00:44:34,240 --> 00:44:36,270
-Osman.
-I'm here.

277
00:44:40,640 --> 00:44:41,770
Ahmet.

278
00:44:45,330 --> 00:44:47,730
-Ahmet...
-What happened to Ahmet?

279
00:44:50,240 --> 00:44:51,980
They took him.

280
00:44:52,730 --> 00:44:54,430
Boran too was captured.

281
00:44:58,140 --> 00:45:00,060
Ahmet is without his mother, Osman.

282
00:45:01,640 --> 00:45:03,650
Don't leave him alone.

283
00:45:04,580 --> 00:45:06,130
Save him from that hell.

284
00:45:10,520 --> 00:45:12,390
Don't worry.

285
00:45:15,340 --> 00:45:17,510
With Allah's approval...

286
00:45:18,230 --> 00:45:20,210
...I will make their lives unbearable.

287
00:45:23,660 --> 00:45:25,120
Rest now.

288
00:45:26,460 --> 00:45:29,950
Rest, so when Ahmet comes back,
he can see you healthy.

289
00:45:36,090 --> 00:45:37,130
My Bala...

290
00:46:03,670 --> 00:46:05,140
Move!

291
00:46:05,300 --> 00:46:06,950
Move!

292
00:46:16,600 --> 00:46:17,800
Move!

293
00:46:19,820 --> 00:46:23,220
While slaughtering everyone else,
why did they bring us here?

294
00:46:25,550 --> 00:46:28,800
They want to use us, dead or alive.

295
00:46:31,530 --> 00:46:32,650
Brother.

296
00:46:33,070 --> 00:46:35,030
Don't you resist them!

297
00:46:35,370 --> 00:46:37,930
Stand tall, don't bow down.

298
00:46:43,800 --> 00:46:47,110
Think about your child.
We will save Ahmet.

299
00:46:53,650 --> 00:46:55,120
Come on.

300
00:46:57,340 --> 00:47:00,230
Ahmet, stay on our back, my lion.

301
00:47:01,310 --> 00:47:02,780
My lion, come on.

302
00:47:04,640 --> 00:47:06,510
We won't resist them.

303
00:47:38,560 --> 00:47:41,680
I wanted to see you in this rathole.

304
00:47:45,170 --> 00:47:49,540
So, you are the closest warriors of
Osman Bey, huh?

305
00:47:50,220 --> 00:47:52,700
Thank Allah, we are like his blood.

306
00:47:56,100 --> 00:47:58,850
Were you with him...

307
00:47:59,460 --> 00:48:03,390
...in Kulucahisar?
-Thank Allah that...

308
00:48:03,400 --> 00:48:06,260
...we were destined to be the veterans
of that battle.

309
00:48:14,810 --> 00:48:16,050
Osman...

310
00:48:17,980 --> 00:48:19,780
Where is Osman?

311
00:48:24,420 --> 00:48:28,120
To rip your heart off, he must be
sharpening his blade.

312
00:48:57,920 --> 00:48:58,980
Father...

313
00:49:05,790 --> 00:49:06,950
Father...

314
00:49:09,570 --> 00:49:11,910
Father, get up, father!

315
00:49:12,570 --> 00:49:14,200
Come on, father!

316
00:49:15,830 --> 00:49:17,770
Come on, father!
Get up, father!

317
00:49:17,930 --> 00:49:20,180
Come on, father!
Come on!

318
00:49:21,670 --> 00:49:22,870
Father!

319
00:49:48,440 --> 00:49:49,350
Father!

320
00:49:52,430 --> 00:49:55,390
Get up, father! Come on, father!
Come on!

321
00:49:57,380 --> 00:49:58,650
Come on!

322
00:50:22,900 --> 00:50:23,900
Die!

323
00:50:29,330 --> 00:50:30,330
Let me go!

324
00:50:30,420 --> 00:50:31,850
Let's go.

325
00:50:32,950 --> 00:50:36,450
I will gift these two to Osman for
Kulucahisar.

326
00:50:46,390 --> 00:50:47,340
Father!

327
00:51:00,780 --> 00:51:03,550
Every single family lost someone...

328
00:51:04,340 --> 00:51:07,940
...they even killed the pregnant
daughter-in-law of Sergeant İlyas.

329
00:51:08,660 --> 00:51:10,930
How did we fall into such a trap, uncle?

330
00:51:12,100 --> 00:51:15,480
It's not the time to grief for the
defeat, brother.

331
00:51:19,500 --> 00:51:22,130
Osman is right, my nephew.
Pull yourself together.

332
00:51:23,020 --> 00:51:24,940
It's time to prepare for revenge.

333
00:51:25,360 --> 00:51:28,000
You are right, uncle. But when?
How?

334
00:51:28,140 --> 00:51:31,790
Tomorrow. An eye for an eye,
a teeth for a teeth.

335
00:51:32,610 --> 00:51:38,020
Does our tent have the strength, Osman?
Do our men or women have the power?

336
00:51:40,670 --> 00:51:44,600
-Let us wait and think about it, nephew.
-What will we think about, uncle?

337
00:51:44,780 --> 00:51:47,410
If we don't move now, we can never
stand up again.

338
00:51:48,600 --> 00:51:51,380
We are knowingly sending the people
to death, Osman!

339
00:51:51,620 --> 00:51:54,460
Let us take a breath. Get stronger,
re-organize.

340
00:51:54,610 --> 00:51:58,200
So that our soldiers can heal, my nephew.

341
00:51:58,730 --> 00:52:03,360
If you were so smart, you should've taken
your measures and prevented it.

342
00:52:12,960 --> 00:52:16,500
If we have a weakness, so do they.

343
00:52:21,540 --> 00:52:24,620
They dealt us a major blow after
a long time.

344
00:52:26,430 --> 00:52:30,000
Now, they all have
the euphoria of victory.

345
00:52:31,960 --> 00:52:36,020
Osman must be thinking that we have
the euphoria of victory now.

346
00:52:36,480 --> 00:52:37,910
-We are.

347
00:52:40,430 --> 00:52:44,650
From now, no one will take a sip.

348
00:52:49,660 --> 00:52:56,030
Everyone will forget the blow we dealt,
and remember cruelty in Kulucahisar.

349
00:52:56,930 --> 00:53:00,960
The ones who forget our slaughtered
children, our destroyed relics...

350
00:53:02,130 --> 00:53:04,430
...should be damned...

351
00:53:05,360 --> 00:53:07,520
...should be a friend to the hellhounds.

352
00:53:08,970 --> 00:53:11,050
What are you thinking?

353
00:53:11,540 --> 00:53:14,110
We will attack them before giving a
chance to recover.

354
00:53:15,280 --> 00:53:18,140
If we give them to take a breath...

355
00:53:19,070 --> 00:53:21,790
...we will be feeding our own monsters.

356
00:53:24,100 --> 00:53:26,250
We will face them tomorrow.

357
00:53:27,350 --> 00:53:29,930
It will be such a great battle that...

358
00:53:31,890 --> 00:53:35,230
All the saints will leave their graves...

359
00:53:36,630 --> 00:53:38,980
...and join our army.

360
00:53:42,330 --> 00:53:44,890
Jesus will come down
to earth...

361
00:53:46,260 --> 00:53:48,500
...and lead our armies.

362
00:53:50,130 --> 00:53:53,560
He must've reinforced his army
with troops from Constantinople.

363
00:53:55,950 --> 00:53:57,450
No doubt.

364
00:53:57,620 --> 00:54:00,500
True. But...

365
00:54:00,690 --> 00:54:03,040
...every army has a weakness.

366
00:54:03,530 --> 00:54:07,860
His army must've rested.
And their morale is boosted.

367
00:54:08,170 --> 00:54:10,910
True. It will shake us.

368
00:54:11,590 --> 00:54:15,120
But, their faith will be their
biggest problem.

369
00:54:16,480 --> 00:54:20,030
Osman, most of our warriors are
wounded, exhausted...

370
00:54:20,790 --> 00:54:24,710
We will reach to their souls.
We will cure their wounds.

371
00:54:31,740 --> 00:54:33,470
-Selamün aleyküm
-Aleyküm selam.

372
00:54:33,580 --> 00:54:38,610
What's the situation, Master Davut?
Though, I know. The warriors aren't fine.

373
00:54:38,870 --> 00:54:42,790
They are wounded. And a lot of
weapons are taken.

374
00:54:44,080 --> 00:54:46,390
How many weapons can you make
until morning?

375
00:54:48,330 --> 00:54:53,370
If you will take revenge from the enemy,
I'll make weapons out of any steel I find.

376
00:54:54,570 --> 00:54:56,760
Just so we can get our revenge soon.

377
00:54:58,510 --> 00:55:01,750
Don't let the path of revenge be our
end.

378
00:55:02,590 --> 00:55:05,880
Revenge is a dish best eaten cold,
my nephew.

379
00:55:06,910 --> 00:55:10,060
Even if not today, it will be
eaten tomorrow.

380
00:55:11,500 --> 00:55:14,430
Strike while the iron is hot, Dündar Bey.

381
00:55:16,520 --> 00:55:20,020
We should strike soon so that their
victory won't be abiding.

382
00:55:22,910 --> 00:55:26,920
We should strike soon so that our
defeat won't be our fear.

383
00:55:28,940 --> 00:55:32,500
We should strike soon so that we can
bury our pain in the ground.

384
00:56:02,940 --> 00:56:09,100
Forge such weapons that our victory
will be the subject of epics.

385
00:56:10,390 --> 00:56:12,270
As you command, my bey.

386
00:56:24,780 --> 00:56:26,350
How are your wounds, brother?

387
00:56:26,670 --> 00:56:28,780
Not as deep as the ones on my heart.

388
00:56:33,430 --> 00:56:35,260
Now listen to me carefully.

389
00:56:46,160 --> 00:56:47,160
All right.

390
00:57:14,030 --> 00:57:18,890
Osman speaks the truth. But if we lose,
we'll return the way we came.

391
00:57:19,380 --> 00:57:23,220
All the efforts, all the struggle, all the
suffering will be for nothing.

392
00:57:23,540 --> 00:57:26,460
I wish we had sent word to my brother,
Yavlak Arslan.

393
00:57:26,710 --> 00:57:28,870
He would come to aid with
his veterans.

394
00:57:29,400 --> 00:57:32,160
We have many wounded warriors.

395
00:57:32,710 --> 00:57:35,400
What if this battle is our disaster?

396
00:57:38,000 --> 00:57:42,190
Be at ease, wife. Tomorrow, such a
storm will break out on those heathens...

397
00:57:42,770 --> 00:57:46,650
Allah who didn't leave the valiants of
Badr alone...

398
00:57:46,650 --> 00:57:49,400
...will come to our aid with the angels.

399
00:57:50,580 --> 00:57:53,520
Mashallah.
Let's begin the preparations, then.

400
00:57:54,490 --> 00:57:59,340
If you don't build a tower from the skulls of
the heathens tomorrow...

401
00:57:59,340 --> 00:58:01,850
...I will die in disappointment.

402
00:58:03,360 --> 00:58:06,030
May you live long, wife.
May you live long.

403
00:58:06,580 --> 00:58:10,400
You brought honor to my tent.

404
00:58:11,330 --> 00:58:13,020
May you live long.

405
00:58:16,790 --> 00:58:19,510
Tomorrow will be a good day.

406
00:58:19,710 --> 00:58:22,200
Castle of İnegöl

407
00:58:43,970 --> 00:58:45,710
Osman has a death wish.

408
00:58:45,890 --> 00:58:48,220
He invites our lord to a battle
to die.

409
00:58:51,100 --> 00:58:53,000
Osman will die!

410
00:59:00,450 --> 00:59:02,100
Guards!

411
00:59:04,690 --> 00:59:06,560
Guards!

412
00:59:09,000 --> 00:59:11,590
With the name of Allah!
With the name of Allah!

413
00:59:34,220 --> 00:59:37,790
With the name of Allah!
With the name of Allah!

414
00:59:48,690 --> 00:59:52,170
I tied your armor so tight
that...

415
00:59:53,230 --> 00:59:55,600
...the heathens' weapons
can't pierce it.

416
00:59:55,900 --> 00:59:58,250
I tied a knot on your steel, my bey...

417
00:59:58,990 --> 01:00:01,830
...as a shield against the spikes that
seek your blood.

418
01:00:03,580 --> 01:00:06,290
For every single drop of blood
they spilled...

419
01:00:06,590 --> 01:00:08,970
...for every life they have taken...

420
01:00:10,500 --> 01:00:11,870
...and for Ahmet...

421
01:00:14,800 --> 01:00:17,330
...I'll leave them no corner to run to
in this world.

422
01:01:23,750 --> 01:01:27,930
My warriors! If we fall, the nation falls!

423
01:01:28,630 --> 01:01:31,770
If we get tired, the state collapses!

424
01:01:33,910 --> 01:01:37,020
If we win, the enemy trembles!

425
01:01:42,680 --> 01:01:43,970
My warriors!

426
01:01:46,870 --> 01:01:48,990
For the love of...

427
01:01:50,500 --> 01:01:52,640
...who makes many out of few...

428
01:01:53,110 --> 01:01:55,920
...who gives us courage!

429
01:01:58,870 --> 01:01:59,950
Today...

430
01:02:00,790 --> 01:02:02,680
...it is a sin to...

431
01:02:03,440 --> 01:02:07,420
...get tired, agrize, drain away...

432
01:02:08,130 --> 01:02:09,790
...or give up!

433
01:02:11,420 --> 01:02:14,280
It is the day of the holy war!

434
01:02:15,130 --> 01:02:16,580
Come on!

435
01:02:17,000 --> 01:02:19,120
Ya Allah!

436
01:03:48,710 --> 01:03:50,550
Allahu Akbar.

437
01:03:56,840 --> 01:03:58,920
Ahmet Alp!
Ahmet Alp!

438
01:04:00,260 --> 01:04:03,310
Do you see it? Didn't I tell you that
Osman Bey would come?

439
01:04:16,700 --> 01:04:18,460
Osman is out of his mind.

440
01:04:18,850 --> 01:04:21,620
Do he think that he can beat
us with that many men?

441
01:04:35,200 --> 01:04:37,310
Osman Bey!

442
01:04:56,440 --> 01:04:57,930
Vile dog!

443
01:05:31,560 --> 01:05:35,370
Don't stand still!
Move! Come on!

444
01:06:53,440 --> 01:06:54,640
Allah!

445
01:06:58,070 --> 01:07:00,890
Göktuğ!
Come on!

446
01:07:20,140 --> 01:07:22,210
Die, Osman!

447
01:07:48,300 --> 01:07:49,990
Charge!

448
01:08:04,860 --> 01:08:07,460
Protect Ahmet!

449
01:09:08,600 --> 01:09:09,910
Let's go, my lions!

450
01:09:13,899 --> 01:09:15,790
Allahu Akbar!

451
01:10:23,530 --> 01:10:24,620
What do we do?

452
01:11:09,340 --> 01:11:10,550
Attack!

453
01:18:34,860 --> 01:18:37,850
Master Davud!
When do you think we'll get some news?

454
01:18:39,290 --> 01:18:41,070
How should I know?

455
01:18:41,260 --> 01:18:43,330
I hope we get good news.

456
01:18:53,240 --> 01:18:55,300
People are full of hope.

457
01:18:55,910 --> 01:18:57,470
They want us to rise.

458
01:18:58,710 --> 01:19:00,740
How will we succeed?

459
01:19:01,200 --> 01:19:05,200
By being Turks
and staying Muslim.

460
01:19:05,200 --> 01:19:08,990
I'd die for this state.

461
01:23:25,710 --> 01:23:27,850
Nobody touches the prisoners.

462
01:23:30,180 --> 01:23:32,170
Take care of the wounded.

463
01:23:33,760 --> 01:23:37,050
They didn't treat us that way, my Bey!
They made us puke blood!

464
01:23:42,230 --> 01:23:43,820
We should be different.

465
01:23:47,050 --> 01:23:49,180
We should be different so that...

466
01:23:53,050 --> 01:23:55,090
... our prophet...

467
01:23:57,310 --> 01:23:59,150
... is proud of us.

468
01:24:00,340 --> 01:24:03,230
Very well, my Bey.

469
01:24:36,230 --> 01:24:37,300
To you...

470
01:24:39,070 --> 01:24:41,600
All glory to you, my Rab(God).

471
01:24:44,080 --> 01:24:46,040
All glory to you.

472
01:25:03,280 --> 01:25:06,070
All glory to you.

473
01:25:56,830 --> 01:25:58,880
My dear Rab!

474
01:26:01,600 --> 01:26:03,690
You gave us power!

475
01:26:05,170 --> 01:26:06,570
You gave us courage.

476
01:26:07,430 --> 01:26:10,230
We were helpless.
You made us powerful!

477
01:26:11,660 --> 01:26:14,660
We were few,
you made us plenty.

478
01:26:16,290 --> 01:26:22,480
My dear Rab!
Protect us from arrogance!

479
01:26:22,480 --> 01:26:24,050
- Amin!
- Amin!

480
01:26:24,050 --> 01:26:27,040
Protect us from arrogance!

481
01:26:27,040 --> 01:26:28,050
- Amin!
- Amin!

482
01:26:28,050 --> 01:26:30,760
Protect us from arrogance!

483
01:26:30,760 --> 01:26:31,830
- Amin!
- Amin!

484
01:26:31,830 --> 01:26:35,970
My dear Rab!
Thank you!

485
01:26:35,970 --> 01:26:37,440
- Thank you!
- Thank you!

486
01:26:37,440 --> 01:26:42,940
- Thanks to you!
- Thank you!

487
01:26:44,470 --> 01:26:52,050
This army, this nation,
shall die for you!

488
01:26:52,050 --> 01:26:53,990
- Shall die for you!
- Shall die for you!

489
01:26:58,380 --> 01:27:00,160
Please, accept our prayers!

490
01:27:00,160 --> 01:27:01,150
- Amin!
- Amin!

491
01:27:01,150 --> 01:27:02,640
Please, accept our prayers!

492
01:27:02,640 --> 01:27:06,130
- Amin!
- Please, accept our prayers!

493
01:27:49,740 --> 01:27:55,520
Eternal justice,
eternal freedom!

494
01:27:59,150 --> 01:28:06,210
- Allahu Akbar!
- Allahu Akbar!

495
01:28:52,470 --> 01:28:55,530
You're the only artist
I get inspirations from.

496
01:29:00,120 --> 01:29:03,780
My only struggle is
to protect your legacy.

497
01:29:04,690 --> 01:29:08,090
I'm fully confident that
I will succeed.

498
01:29:10,650 --> 01:29:14,130
You're the greatest example of
how hard one becomes an artist.

499
01:29:20,350 --> 01:29:22,840
I admire your ability
to overcome problems.

500
01:29:24,910 --> 01:29:27,940
You never gave up.
Never!

501
01:29:31,920 --> 01:29:38,080
Mighty Ceasar! Your greatest work
is the Roman Empire!

502
01:29:38,620 --> 01:29:42,360
Your greatest work, created by
shedding the blood of the enemy...

503
01:29:42,360 --> 01:29:46,690
... by showing no mercy to traitors,
heartening the cowards!

504
01:29:47,430 --> 01:29:52,260
Mighty Ceasar! Rome
is fighting for its life today!

505
01:29:52,260 --> 01:29:55,860
The Roman Empire is under the attack
of barbarians!

506
01:29:55,860 --> 01:30:02,070
Its leaders are destroying
Rome from the inside!

507
01:30:02,260 --> 01:30:06,260
I am Aya Nikola! I promise!

508
01:30:06,460 --> 01:30:10,460
I'll recreate the big and
powerful Roman Empire!

509
01:30:18,310 --> 01:30:22,680
Salute, soldier!
Salute the mighty Ceasar!

510
01:30:31,120 --> 01:30:34,840
My magical fingers have recreated Ceasar.

511
01:30:35,730 --> 01:30:37,900
Flawless.

512
01:30:40,720 --> 01:30:42,630
The Emperor is waiting for you.

513
01:30:53,300 --> 01:30:55,130
Mighty Ceasar...

514
01:30:56,290 --> 01:30:58,230
At last...

515
01:31:07,430 --> 01:31:10,020
Alexis, governor of İnegöl.

516
01:31:10,340 --> 01:31:12,870
As if getting defeated by the
Kayıs is not enough...

517
01:31:12,870 --> 01:31:16,690
... he ran away from the battle like a rat
and hid in his castle.

518
01:31:16,820 --> 01:31:22,180
- How could he do that?
- How dare him!

519
01:31:22,990 --> 01:31:27,980
What comes after Karacahisar
and Kulacahisar castles?

520
01:31:28,850 --> 01:31:32,850
İznik? Bursa?
Or...

521
01:31:32,960 --> 01:31:34,860
... Constantinople?

522
01:31:43,510 --> 01:31:44,760
Enough!

523
01:31:48,130 --> 01:31:51,660
Just like we beat the crusader
army off of our city...

524
01:31:52,150 --> 01:31:55,050
... it's time we beat off
the Turks as well.

525
01:31:55,260 --> 01:32:00,150
I only have one commander in my empire
who I believe can do this.

526
01:32:01,260 --> 01:32:03,140
Invite him to the council.

527
01:32:39,740 --> 01:32:41,220
Emperor.

528
01:32:47,540 --> 01:32:50,060
Honourable members of the council.

529
01:32:55,610 --> 01:32:57,600
You know why you were invited.

530
01:32:58,710 --> 01:33:00,200
Because you are sick...

531
01:33:03,560 --> 01:33:05,270
... and tired...

532
01:33:06,060 --> 01:33:08,380
... of cowardice and betrayal!

533
01:33:10,230 --> 01:33:12,240
So that I could end...

534
01:33:15,530 --> 01:33:17,100
... the harassments of the enemy!

535
01:33:18,850 --> 01:33:24,520
You called me so that I can introduce my
iron fist to the east of our Empire!

536
01:33:32,360 --> 01:33:34,410
But...!

537
01:33:36,120 --> 01:33:37,690
But...

538
01:33:38,570 --> 01:33:40,280
Under two conditions.

539
01:33:41,920 --> 01:33:45,730
If you allow me to...

540
01:33:48,050 --> 01:33:54,420
I'll take back the Kulacahisar
Osman Bey took.

541
01:33:55,580 --> 01:34:00,790
I'll also take back the Karacahisar
his father took.

542
01:34:04,160 --> 01:34:09,800
But this won't annihilate
the danger of Turks.

543
01:34:10,060 --> 01:34:14,140
Of course, you'll applaud,
drown me in gold and raise my rank.

544
01:34:14,140 --> 01:34:18,060
But this small gift I'll be giving
you will not stop...

545
01:34:18,060 --> 01:34:23,520
... our melting like snow on a mountain
summit on a hot day.

546
01:34:27,300 --> 01:34:29,690
What's your offer, Nikola?

547
01:34:33,320 --> 01:34:41,600
I want full command of all the governors,
soldiers, patrol units in the area.

548
01:34:42,700 --> 01:34:44,520
Full authority.

549
01:34:49,790 --> 01:34:53,020
Not to take back the castles
we have lost.

550
01:34:54,410 --> 01:34:57,720
To take back everything...

551
01:34:59,760 --> 01:35:03,960
To take back everything we have lost.

552
01:35:04,770 --> 01:35:09,720
Our lands, churches, villages, bridges...

553
01:35:10,690 --> 01:35:13,360
To take back the honour we have lost.

554
01:35:14,430 --> 01:35:17,350
Long story short...

555
01:35:19,570 --> 01:35:25,710
I want unlimited authority to take
back the spirit we have lost.

556
01:35:27,050 --> 01:35:28,470
Emperor.

557
01:35:48,130 --> 01:35:50,040
What about the second condition?

558
01:35:58,520 --> 01:36:02,520
I gather my own men.

559
01:36:06,170 --> 01:36:08,000
The leader of this team...

560
01:36:08,000 --> 01:36:13,940
... will be Flatyus. Your greatest enemy.

561
01:37:04,980 --> 01:37:06,650
Don't you have food?

562
01:37:07,390 --> 01:37:08,490
We're hungry!

563
01:38:01,120 --> 01:38:05,690
No. I can't sit here and wait.
We need a solution.

564
01:38:06,810 --> 01:38:08,070
What solution?

565
01:38:08,070 --> 01:38:12,510
We need a solution to quickly inform those
who are expecting news!

566
01:38:22,410 --> 01:38:24,960
Master Davud!

567
01:38:37,300 --> 01:38:39,060
Thank you, my Allah!

568
01:38:39,130 --> 01:38:40,660
My lions!

569
01:38:43,170 --> 01:38:46,640
- Praise be!
- Praise be! Thank you, my Allah!

570
01:38:46,640 --> 01:38:49,230
- Move!
- Thank you, my Rab(God)!

571
01:39:10,440 --> 01:39:12,280
Make way!

572
01:39:19,260 --> 01:39:21,170
Are we victorious?

573
01:39:22,910 --> 01:39:26,690
Thank you, my Rab!
Thank you!

574
01:39:48,960 --> 01:39:52,220
May Allah bless you with many victories!

575
01:40:23,830 --> 01:40:25,150
My Ahmet!

576
01:40:26,290 --> 01:40:28,830
How many heathens did you slice,
my Ahmet?

577
01:40:43,750 --> 01:40:45,730
I'd die for you!

578
01:41:47,510 --> 01:41:48,860
Look at me.

579
01:41:51,330 --> 01:41:53,330
My father became a martyr!

580
01:41:55,000 --> 01:41:56,850
My father became a martyr!

581
01:43:14,390 --> 01:43:16,790
You are here safe and sound.

582
01:43:16,790 --> 01:43:19,220
We are so grateful.

583
01:43:19,220 --> 01:43:23,050
Praise be, Gonca Hatun, praise be.

584
01:43:25,350 --> 01:43:31,000
Thank my Allah, who granted us with
this victory.

585
01:43:31,000 --> 01:43:32,800
Amin!

586
01:43:32,800 --> 01:43:36,930
My valiants!
I will cut it short.

587
01:43:37,920 --> 01:43:42,960
- Thank heaven, we defeated the enemy!
- Thank heaven.

588
01:43:42,960 --> 01:43:45,820
Thank heaven.

589
01:43:46,570 --> 01:43:51,930
Now, we need to defeat our nafs!
(self ego)

590
01:43:52,640 --> 01:43:54,210
Eyvallah.
(Thanks)

591
01:46:00,490 --> 01:46:03,560
Our friendship ends here.

592
01:46:09,840 --> 01:46:12,150
Forgive me.

593
01:47:21,870 --> 01:47:25,570
Constantine.

594
01:47:26,680 --> 01:47:31,020
My dear friend, Constantine
resurrecting!

595
01:47:35,320 --> 01:47:37,660
What is happening there?

596
01:47:44,330 --> 01:47:46,250
What is that?

597
01:47:46,250 --> 01:47:48,280
Let me introduce you...

598
01:47:48,800 --> 01:47:51,240
Constantine.

599
01:48:04,850 --> 01:48:07,590
He is escaping!

600
01:48:49,170 --> 01:48:54,720
Constantine, my dear friend.
I am grateful.

601
01:51:15,140 --> 01:51:17,010
Nicola.

602
01:51:27,360 --> 01:51:30,530
How great it is to see you after
so many years.

603
01:51:38,560 --> 01:51:42,450
I guess dungeons couldn't break you.

604
01:51:43,010 --> 01:51:45,830
Revenge fed me.

605
01:51:54,510 --> 01:51:57,810
I came to give you a new mission.

606
01:51:59,460 --> 01:52:01,940
In the day I am escaping?

607
01:52:05,370 --> 01:52:07,610
Get away.

608
01:52:39,530 --> 01:52:42,750
You didn't stop those viles who
put me in there!

609
01:52:51,800 --> 01:52:55,260
Thank you, friend. You saved my life.

610
01:52:55,260 --> 01:52:57,870
I completed my mission, Nikola.

611
01:52:59,880 --> 01:53:03,840
If you don't have a command, I'd like
to return to my duty.

612
01:53:12,980 --> 01:53:16,600
I used to knew every pain
you'd gone through.

613
01:53:17,670 --> 01:53:20,460
I used to know every meal you'd had.

614
01:53:20,460 --> 01:53:22,050
I came here.

615
01:53:22,290 --> 01:53:28,230
I came here and wanted to see if my
efforts went down to drain or not.

616
01:53:29,700 --> 01:53:33,140
I hope I didn't let you know.

617
01:53:34,780 --> 01:53:39,980
But, don't forget that Flatyos is
nobody's dog!

618
01:54:15,140 --> 01:54:20,430
Flatyus! I offer you destroying Ertuğrul
and Kayıs!

619
01:54:42,810 --> 01:54:44,190
My God.

620
01:54:45,020 --> 01:54:46,760
Finally...

621
01:54:47,240 --> 01:54:48,900
Finally...

622
01:54:54,750 --> 01:54:57,470
İnegöl Castle
4 days after...

623
01:55:29,610 --> 01:55:31,540
Nikola.

624
01:55:45,100 --> 01:55:48,520
Emperor heard us, and sent you.

625
01:55:48,520 --> 01:55:50,800
For christ's sake!

626
01:55:51,180 --> 01:55:54,400
Today is going to be our salvation day.

627
01:55:55,720 --> 01:55:57,780
Welcome.

628
01:55:57,780 --> 01:56:00,250
Welcome my old friend.

629
01:56:00,920 --> 01:56:05,940
Were they with you while you were
running away from Kayıs, Alexis?

630
01:56:09,810 --> 01:56:13,940
Are you here to question us or help us?

631
01:56:20,440 --> 01:56:23,110
To question you.

632
01:56:26,860 --> 01:56:29,780
But not you.

633
01:56:34,250 --> 01:56:36,870
It's Kayıs.

634
01:56:59,130 --> 01:57:02,340
I brought you a gift, Alexis.

635
01:57:02,450 --> 01:57:04,860
I hope you like it.

636
01:57:07,540 --> 01:57:09,360
Thank you, Nikola.

637
01:57:09,500 --> 01:57:13,710
I hope you like the meal which I
have it prepared.

638
01:57:13,710 --> 01:57:19,630
It's your favourite meal, Pork stew
with beans. I didn't forget.

639
01:57:19,980 --> 01:57:21,940
I like it.

640
01:57:42,430 --> 01:57:44,640
Traitor!

641
01:57:59,480 --> 01:58:06,050
Supreme Caesar. my first action is to
clear the idiots in our castle.

642
01:58:06,740 --> 01:58:10,680
I feel honored to present you.

643
01:58:44,440 --> 01:58:46,940
I don't like cowards.

644
01:59:39,480 --> 01:59:45,700
Kneel in front of New İnegöl Governor
Aya Nikola!

645
01:59:53,930 --> 01:59:57,060
Now it's time to clear the enemies
outside the castle.

646
01:59:57,090 --> 02:00:03,940
In a short time, with my will and soul
of Helen, a brand new Roma will rise!

647
02:00:05,150 --> 02:00:09,580
May Jesus bless you, Governor Nikola.

648
02:00:10,330 --> 02:00:14,800
Bless all of us, father, all of us.

649
02:00:49,170 --> 02:00:51,030
Bala.

650
02:00:51,530 --> 02:00:54,070
What are you doing?

651
02:00:54,970 --> 02:00:59,070
While I am standing here? No.

652
02:01:05,080 --> 02:01:09,520
I want you to come to the table
that I prepared myself, Osman.

653
02:01:09,520 --> 02:01:14,880
You are tired of fighting, please grant me
this honor.

654
02:01:16,030 --> 02:01:17,900
Oooohhh...

655
02:01:18,540 --> 02:01:21,350
My sweet Bala.

656
02:01:21,610 --> 02:01:25,530
You already honored me by taking
a huge place in my heart.

657
02:01:29,410 --> 02:01:31,850
Besides, I can set the table very well.

658
02:01:32,190 --> 02:01:34,870
Come on, sit.

659
02:01:36,400 --> 02:01:39,700
Osman Bey, can I?

660
02:01:43,150 --> 02:01:45,210
Come.

661
02:02:12,390 --> 02:02:14,490
What is new?

662
02:02:14,590 --> 02:02:18,590
Ertuğrul Bey.
News from Ertuğrul Bey.

663
02:02:23,540 --> 02:02:26,550
Dündar Bey invites you to his tent.

664
02:02:35,690 --> 02:02:37,430
My Osman.

665
02:02:38,890 --> 02:02:41,480
May it be good, my Osman.

666
02:02:41,600 --> 02:02:46,340
Fast, fast, bring the clothes fast.

667
02:04:30,660 --> 02:04:32,960
What's it about my father, uncle?

668
02:04:33,370 --> 02:04:37,550
Kuzgun Bey from Cobanogullari.

669
02:04:39,920 --> 02:04:43,990
- Welcome Kuzgun Bey.
- I have news from Ertuğrul Bey.

670
02:04:44,240 --> 02:04:48,340
May Allah be pleased of you, you
brought good news from my father.

671
02:04:48,340 --> 02:04:50,140
Eyvallah, Osman Bey.
(thank you)

672
02:04:50,140 --> 02:04:56,780
Yavlak Arslan and Ertuğrul Bey will meet
in Kastamonu and evaluate Byzantine.

673
02:04:58,260 --> 02:05:02,930
- Ertuğrul Bey is waiting in Badembükü.
- Is my brother fine?

674
02:05:03,230 --> 02:05:06,740
Fine enough to break infidels.

675
02:05:06,740 --> 02:05:08,830
Masha Allah.

676
02:05:08,830 --> 02:05:10,900
Masha Allah. (praise be)

677
02:05:10,910 --> 02:05:14,890
Then, let me set off immediately.

678
02:05:14,890 --> 02:05:20,050
Ertuğrul Bey wants Osman alone.
I was commanded that.

679
02:05:20,660 --> 02:05:27,790
Bey of the Beys Yavlak Hasan also wants to
see Osman who became legend in wars.

680
02:05:30,170 --> 02:05:34,750
Ertuğrul Bey wants to set off from
Gündoğan tomorrow morning.

681
02:05:41,420 --> 02:05:46,220
You brought happiness, Kuzgun Bey.
You made us happy.

682
02:05:46,220 --> 02:05:51,460
Eyvallah, I completed my duty,
brought the news.

683
02:05:51,540 --> 02:05:53,520
Excuse me.

684
02:06:13,780 --> 02:06:16,940
Do you know Kidigon River, Flatyus?

685
02:06:25,850 --> 02:06:30,310
The river that Julia Caesar passed with
his legions...

686
02:06:30,310 --> 02:06:34,270
to become Emperor by conquering Rome.

687
02:06:35,020 --> 02:06:38,750
Not Emperor.
A god.

688
02:06:38,750 --> 02:06:41,940
He was a God.

689
02:06:47,700 --> 02:06:53,440
His heart flows in this land's water.

690
02:06:53,910 --> 02:06:56,280
In Sakarya river.

691
02:06:57,280 --> 02:07:03,310
When the time comes, I will cross
that river.

692
02:07:07,530 --> 02:07:10,250
That river, Flatyus...

693
02:07:12,260 --> 02:07:16,500
is going to make me the Emperor of Rome.

694
02:07:20,210 --> 02:07:24,900
Did I tell that I was baptized in Sakarya
River?

695
02:07:31,540 --> 02:07:38,430
From that day, every river in world
flows in my body.

696
02:07:53,710 --> 02:07:56,760
Just like Julia Caesar.

697
02:07:56,760 --> 02:08:01,560
It resembles you more than him.

698
02:08:11,070 --> 02:08:14,440
Can you spot any difference?

699
02:08:24,930 --> 02:08:27,290
I can't.
What is...

700
02:08:28,040 --> 02:08:33,260
Lots of death is
hidden in this little box.

701
02:08:33,270 --> 02:08:37,210
First Söğüt, then Karacahisar.

702
02:08:37,210 --> 02:08:44,020
First tears, and then blood will be there,
in every place Turks conquered.

703
02:08:44,860 --> 02:08:46,640
Then...

704
02:08:52,620 --> 02:08:55,960
Our we will climb our victory ladder,
Flatyus.

705
02:09:24,990 --> 02:09:27,790
To our victory.

706
02:09:57,650 --> 02:10:02,450
Are you too confused that only
Osman was invited by Ertuğrul Bey, my Bey?

707
02:10:06,790 --> 02:10:09,900
Do you think he should have
invited me, Hazal?

708
02:10:10,770 --> 02:10:17,030
Of course he should have, Dündar Bey.
You are Ertuğrul Ghazi's brother.

709
02:10:17,710 --> 02:10:21,880
You are the honorable Bey of this tribe.

710
02:10:23,510 --> 02:10:28,870
May Allah give my lifespan to my brother.

711
02:10:28,870 --> 02:10:34,340
However, I don't know how I will
look at his eyes...

712
02:10:34,560 --> 02:10:37,140
when he comes here.

713
02:10:37,240 --> 02:10:40,510
Past is past, Dündar Bey.

714
02:10:41,060 --> 02:10:46,990
If he was going to say something,
you'd know that.

715
02:10:47,270 --> 02:10:54,610
Also, Ertuğrul Ghazi's compassion is as
famous as his justice.

716
02:10:54,850 --> 02:10:59,820
His justice is famous too, Hatun.

717
02:11:00,170 --> 02:11:02,860
I have no doubt.

718
02:11:03,550 --> 02:11:10,060
However, I don't understand why Osman
goes while you are here.

719
02:11:10,060 --> 02:11:15,880
You have experience, you are valiant.

720
02:11:17,270 --> 02:11:21,410
Both wisdom and administration is
in Ertuğrul Ghazi.

721
02:11:21,410 --> 02:11:24,940
He knows what to do the best.

722
02:13:24,000 --> 02:13:26,540
My Ertuğrul Bey.

723
02:13:27,160 --> 02:13:31,580
My Ertuğrul Bey.
My Ertuğrul Bey is coming!

724
02:14:17,060 --> 02:14:19,390
Brother!

725
02:14:24,070 --> 02:14:25,980
My father.

726
02:15:26,740 --> 02:15:28,520
My Father.

727
02:15:30,150 --> 02:15:33,320
- Welcome, father.
- Thank you.

728
02:15:33,320 --> 02:15:37,120
Welcome, brother, welcome.

729
02:15:39,130 --> 02:15:42,360
I have longed for you all.

730
02:15:47,230 --> 02:15:49,920
Thank you brother.

731
02:16:02,490 --> 02:16:04,640
My Bey.

732
02:16:13,150 --> 02:16:15,370
Where is Osman?

733
02:16:22,510 --> 02:16:25,330
I can't see Osman.

734
02:16:35,020 --> 02:16:39,139
- Didn't you call Osman?
- What are you talking about, Dündar?

735
02:16:44,270 --> 02:16:46,620
Where is Osman?

736
02:17:30,600 --> 02:17:32,520
Osman...

737
02:17:32,972 --> 02:17:35,181
I thought Osman was with you, my Bey.

738
02:17:36,928 --> 02:17:39,245
Why did you think that, Gündüz?

739
02:17:40,018 --> 02:17:42,067
-What's happening here?
-My Bey.

740
02:17:42,096 --> 02:17:45,173
Yesterday, Yavlak Arslan's chamberlain,
Kuzgun Bey was here.

741
02:17:45,538 --> 02:17:48,488
He said that you summoned Osman Bey.

742
02:18:00,614 --> 02:18:03,204
No one knew that I would come
to the tents.

743
02:18:31,563 --> 02:18:35,163
The secret is revealed.

744
02:18:36,215 --> 02:18:39,129
Cain killed Abel and the secret got
revealed.

745
02:18:42,517 --> 02:18:44,567
The earth cried. It cried, indeed.

746
02:18:46,412 --> 02:18:49,872
Tears became a flood.

747
02:18:50,761 --> 02:18:53,459
There were the floods, the floods!

748
02:18:54,274 --> 02:18:57,110
Mountains turned into islands,
plains turned into seas.

749
02:18:57,403 --> 02:19:02,095
A voice was heard in the flood,
''Give me your hand, give me your hand!''

750
02:19:02,934 --> 02:19:05,753
''What are you waiting for, my child?
Give me your hand!''

751
02:19:05,949 --> 02:19:09,192
''Please, don't make your father sad.
Give me your hand!''

752
02:19:09,783 --> 02:19:14,631
''Give me your hand, son. Give me your
hand! Look, Father Noah wants you.''

753
02:19:17,979 --> 02:19:22,477
''How can a father not spare his son.
Give your hand, give your hand!''

754
02:19:22,477 --> 02:19:26,987
''The waves will eat you, give me your
hand! Give me your hand!''

755
02:19:36,660 --> 02:19:39,230
Son didn't give his hand.

756
02:19:43,520 --> 02:19:46,500
Father Noah cried.

757
02:19:48,530 --> 02:19:51,990
One tear dropped into the sea.

758
02:19:52,370 --> 02:19:58,360
The flood showed mercy and guided
Father Noah to security.

759
02:20:02,340 --> 02:20:07,620
Hey, love, tell me.

760
02:20:09,520 --> 02:20:12,150
Who is the father?

761
02:20:16,020 --> 02:20:18,580
Who is the son?

